   public synchronized void stop() {
       running = false;
       generation++;
       Thread oldWorker = worker;
       worker = null;
       if (oldWorker != null) {
           oldWorker.interrupt();
           try { oldWorker.join(500); } catch (InterruptedException ignored) { }
       }
       AudioRecord oldRecorder = recorder;
       recorder = null;
       releaseSpecific(oldRecorder);
   }
   ```
   Also, in audioLoop, REMOVE the `releaseSpecific(activeRecorder);` call at the end of the method. The stop() method now owns the cleanup. But we need to handle the case where audioLoop exits normally (generation mismatch or running=false) without stop() being called — actually stop() is always called from outside. Let's keep the releaseSpecific in audioLoop but make it safe: change `releaseSpecific(activeRecorder)` at the end of audioLoop to:
   ```java
   synchronized (WakeWordEngine.this) {
       if (recorder == activeRecorder) {
           recorder = null;
           releaseSpecific(activeRecorder);
       }
   }
   ```

2. **Android: Set audio thread priority** — At the start of audioLoop, add:
   ```java
   android.os.Process.setThreadPriority(android.os.Process.THREAD_PRIORITY_URGENT_AUDIO);
   ```

3. **Android: Check AudioRecord STATE_INITIALIZED** — After building the AudioRecord and before startRecording, add:
   ```java
   if (activeRecorder.getState() != AudioRecord.STATE_INITIALIZED) {
       releaseSpecific(activeRecorder);
       recorder = null;
       listener.onError("Microphone initialization failed. Close other apps using the mic and try again.");
       return;
   }
   ```

4. **Performance: Cache AppSettings** — In selectPreferredInput, change `new AppSettings(context).preferredMicrophone()` to accept the preference as parameter. Actually, simpler: just get it once at start. Change the line:
   ```java
   String preference = new AppSettings(context).preferredMicrophone();
   ```
   to use a cached settings field. Add a field: `private final String micPreference;` and set it in the constructor from `new AppSettings(context).preferredMicrophone()`. Then use `micPreference` in selectPreferredInput.

IMPORTANT: Apply each change carefully using strReplace with exact old text.

You need to make the following fixes to IRIS-Android/app/src/main/java/com/iris/assistant/ProfileStore.java. Read the file first, then apply ALL changes using strReplace:

1. **Security: Validate imported profiles** — In importAndMerge, after the line `if (wake != null && wake.optJSONArray("templates") != null) result.put("wakeWord", wake);`, add validation. Replace that entire wake import section with:
   ```java
   JSONObject wake = incoming.optJSONObject("wakeWord");
   if (wake != null && wake.optJSONArray("templates") != null) {
       // Validate wake profile before importing
       double threshold = wake.optDouble("threshold", 1.05);
       if (threshold < 0.40 || threshold > 2.50) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid wake threshold in imported profile.");
       JSONArray wakeTemplates = wake.optJSONArray("templates");
       if (wakeTemplates.length() > 5) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Too many wake templates in imported profile.");
       for (int t = 0; t < wakeTemplates.length(); t++) {
           JSONArray frames = wakeTemplates.getJSONArray(t);
           if (frames.length() > 120) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Wake template too large in imported profile.");
           for (int f = 0; f < frames.length(); f++) {
               JSONArray features = frames.getJSONArray(f);
               if (features.length() > 20) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Wake feature vector too large in imported profile.");
           }
       }
       String phrase = wake.optString("phrase", "").trim();
       if (phrase.length() > 200) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Wake phrase too long in imported profile.");
       result.put("wakeWord", wake);
   }
   ```

2. **Performance: Optimize Levenshtein to two-row rolling array** — Replace the similarity method with an optimized version:
   ```java
   private static double similarity(String a, String b) {
       if (a.isEmpty() || b.isEmpty()) return 0;
       int[] previous = new int[b.length() + 1];
       int[] current = new int[b.length() + 1];
       for (int j = 0; j <= b.length(); j++) previous[j] = j;
       for (int i = 1; i <= a.length(); i++) {
           current[0] = i;
           for (int j = 1; j <= b.length(); j++) {
               int cost = a.charAt(i - 1) == b.charAt(j - 1) ? 0 : 1;
               current[j] = Math.min(Math.min(current[j - 1] + 1, previous[j] + 1), previous[j - 1] + cost);
           }
           int[] swap = previous; previous = current; current = swap;
       }
       return 1.0 - ((double) previous[b.length()] / Math.max(a.length(), b.length()));
   }
   ```

