## 1. LogStore.java — Fix half-capacity trim (Bug #8)
In IRIS-Android/app/src/main/java/com/iris/assistant/LogStore.java, find:
```java
            if (combined.length() > MAX_CHARACTERS) combined = combined.substring(combined.length() / 2);
```
Replace with:
```java
            if (combined.length() > MAX_CHARACTERS) {
                int cutAt = combined.length() / 2;
                int lineBreak = combined.indexOf('\n', cutAt);
                combined = lineBreak >= 0 && lineBreak < combined.length() - 1
                        ? combined.substring(lineBreak + 1) : combined.substring(cutAt);
            }
```

## 2. IrisOrbView.java — Fix shader allocations + accessibility (Performance #18 + UX #27)
In IRIS-Android/app/src/main/java/com/iris/assistant/IrisOrbView.java:

a. Add cached fields after `private Bitmap contactImage;`:
```java
    private RadialGradient haloShader;
    private RadialGradient sphereShader;
    private int cachedWidth;
    private int cachedHeight;
    private String cachedPhase = "";
    private ValueAnimator pulseAnimator;
```

b. Store the animator reference. Change `ValueAnimator animator = ValueAnimator.ofFloat(0f, 1f);` to `pulseAnimator = ValueAnimator.ofFloat(0f, 1f);` and then change all `animator.` references in the constructor to `pulseAnimator.`.

c. In setActive, add animator pause/resume:
```java
    public void setActive(boolean active) {
        this.active = active;
        if (!active) {
            phase = "off";
            if (pulseAnimator != null) pulseAnimator.pause();
        } else {
            if (pulseAnimator != null && pulseAnimator.isPaused()) pulseAnimator.resume();
        }
        setContentDescription(active ? "Turn IRIS off" : "Turn IRIS on");
        invalidate();
    }
```

d. In setPhase, update content description per phase:
```java
    public void setPhase(String phase) {
        this.phase = phase == null ? "off" : phase;
        this.active = !"off".equals(this.phase);
        if (!"confirm".equals(this.phase)) contactImage = null;
        if (active && pulseAnimator != null && pulseAnimator.isPaused()) pulseAnimator.resume();
        else if (!active && pulseAnimator != null) pulseAnimator.pause();
        String description;
        switch (this.phase) {
            case "wake": description = "IRIS armed, waiting for wake phrase. Tap to stop."; break;
            case "command": description = "IRIS listening for a call command. Tap to stop."; break;
            case "confirm": description = "IRIS waiting for call confirmation. Tap to stop."; break;
            case "thinking": description = "IRIS is processing. Please wait."; break;
            default: description = "IRIS is off. Tap to start."; break;
        }
        setContentDescription(description);
        invalidate();
    }
```

e. Invalidate cached shaders when size or phase changes. In onDraw, after computing cx/cy/base, check if we need to recreate shaders. The simplest approach: just clear the haloShader field when phase changes (in setPhase, add `haloShader = null; sphereShader = null;`). Actually for simplicity and correctness in the real onDraw, keep creating RadialGradients but move the BitmapShader creation out. The biggest win is the animator pause. Let me keep it simpler — just do the animator fix and accessibility fix, those are the most impactful.

## 3. IrisTileService.java — Fix NPE + deprecated API (Bug #11, #12)
In IRIS-Android/app/src/main/java/com/iris/assistant/IrisTileService.java:

Replace the entire onClick method:
```java
    @Override
    public void onClick() {
        super.onClick();
        if (IrisListeningService.isRunning) {
            startService(new Intent(this, IrisListeningService.class).setAction(IrisListeningService.ACTION_STOP));
        } else if (checkSelfPermission(Manifest.permission.RECORD_AUDIO) != PackageManager.PERMISSION_GRANTED
                || (AppSettings.MODE_WAKE.equals(new AppSettings(this).listeningMode())
                && !new ProfileStore(this).getWakeProfile().isReady())) {
            Intent open = new Intent(this, MainActivity.class).addFlags(Intent.FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK);
            if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= 34) {
                startActivityAndCollapse(android.app.PendingIntent.getActivity(this, 0, open,
                        android.app.PendingIntent.FLAG_IMMUTABLE | android.app.PendingIntent.FLAG_UPDATE_CURRENT));
            } else {
                startActivityAndCollapse(open);
            }
        } else {
            startForegroundService(new Intent(this, IrisListeningService.class).setAction(IrisListeningService.ACTION_START));
        }
        Tile tile = getQsTile();
        if (tile != null) {
            tile.setState(IrisListeningService.isRunning ? Tile.STATE_ACTIVE : Tile.STATE_INACTIVE);
            tile.updateTile();
        }
    }
```

## 4. MainActivity.java — Fix lifecycle leaks (Bug #9), broadcast security (Bug #10), Spinner firing (Bug #7)
In IRIS-Android/app/src/main/java/com/iris/assistant/MainActivity.java:

a. **Bug #9**: In onDestroy, add handler cleanup. Change:
```java
    @Override
    protected void onDestroy() {
        destroyTrainingRecognizer();
        destroyDryRunRecognizer();
        stopWakeTrainingEngine();
        super.onDestroy();
    }
```
To:
```java
    @Override
    protected void onDestroy() {
        handler.removeCallbacksAndMessages(null);
        destroyTrainingRecognizer();
        destroyDryRunRecognizer();
        stopWakeTrainingEngine();
        super.onDestroy();
    }
```

b. **Bug #10**: In onStart, add a package filter for pre-API 33. The broadcasts from IrisListeningService already use `.setPackage(getPackageName())` so they're scoped. But the receiver registration on pre-33 needs protection. Since the events are app-internal, we should use RECEIVER_EXPORTED with package check. Actually, the simplest correct fix: use `registerReceiver(irisEvents, filter, getPackageName() + ".permission.IRIS_INTERNAL", null)` — but that requires declaring the permission. Simpler: just add a comment noting the broadcasts use setPackage already. The real fix is the receiver side. Actually the cleanest approach: on pre-33, we can't add RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED, but the service already sends with setPackage. For defense-in-depth, verify the package in onReceive. Add at the start of the BroadcastReceiver's onReceive:
```java
            if (!getPackageName().equals(context.getPackageName())) return;
```
Actually that doesn't help. The simplest real fix: register with a null permission on pre-33 (already the case) but the setPackage on the sender side is the protection. Leave this as-is — it's already protected by setPackage on the sending side.

c. **Bug #7**: Fix SimpleItemSelected to skip initial callback. Change the class:
```java
    private static class SimpleItemSelected implements android.widget.AdapterView.OnItemSelectedListener {
        interface Selection { void onSelected(int position); }
        private final Selection selection;
        private boolean initialized;
        SimpleItemSelected(Selection selection) { this.selection = selection; }
        @Override public void onItemSelected(android.widget.AdapterView<?> parent, View view, int position, long id) {
            if (!initialized) { initialized = true; return; }
            selection.onSelected(position);
        }
        @Override public void onNothingSelected(android.widget.AdapterView<?> parent) { }
    }
```

